  "facts": [
    "Opened on May 24, 1883, the Brooklyn Bridge was the first fixed crossing of the East River and held the title of the longest suspension bridge in the world at that time.",
    "Designed by John A. Roebling, the Brooklyn Bridge features a unique hybrid design that combines elements of both cable-stayed and suspension bridges, showcasing neo-Gothic stone towers with pointed arches.",
    "The Brooklyn Bridge's main span measures an impressive 1,595.5 feet long, and its deck is elevated 127 feet above mean high water, allowing for ample clearance for shipping traffic."
